# .gitignore for the PUBLIC palayax/DFIR repository (the analysis web app).
#
# Generated: this file is maintained as build/publish/gitignore in the source
# repo and copied to .gitignore by scripts/publish-web.sh. Edit it there.

# The app is dependency-free by design. Their presence is a regression, and
# .github/workflows/pages.yml fails the build if either is committed.
node_modules/
package-lock.json
npm-debug.log*

# MUST NEVER be committed: real collection output contains a real host's
# forensic evidence (registry hives, event logs, file contents, process lists).
# The only timeline data in this repo is web/fixtures/, which is synthetic and
# regenerated by web/fixtures/generate-fixtures.mjs (hosts WKS-CORP-01/02,
# users DOMAIN\alice / DOMAIN\bob).
IRTriage_*.zip
*_timeline.csv
*_timeline.jsonl
/timeline.csv
/timeline.jsonl
collections/

# Analysis output can quote evidence verbatim and may name real hosts/users.
supertimeline*.jsonl
supertimeline*.csv
report-*.json
report-*.pdf

# Secrets. The app keeps LLM/storage API keys in memory, with opt-in AES-GCM
# encrypted persistence under a user passphrase. Nothing here should ever exist,
# but defence in depth on a public repo is cheap.
*.key
*.pem
.env
.env.*
credentials.json
secrets.yaml
*token*.txt

# OS / editor
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*~
*.swp
